    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22195" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ăquōsus</span></b> 
		a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>lacking water</i>
			 (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">loca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Hist. Eccl. 1, 1</span></i>
			: inaquosus <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνυδρος,</span> Gloss.
			Cyril.— As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnăquōsa</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n.
			plur., <i>dry places</i>, <i>desert places</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">serpentes arida et inaquosa sectantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Bapt. 1</span></i>
			.</div>
